User: /speckit.specify Build a Library Book-Loan Service exposed as a JSON HTTP API.

Entities:
- Book: id, title, author, isbn (13 digits), total_copies
- Member: id, name, email
- Loan: id, book_id, member_id, loaned_at, due_date, returned_at

Business rules:
- The loan period is 14 days from the loan date.
- A member may have at most 3 active (unreturned) loans.
- A book can be loaned only if available copies > 0.
- Available copies = total_copies minus active loans for that book.

Acceptance criteria (each must be testable as pass/fail):
AC-1: POST /books with valid title, author, 13-digit isbn and total_copies >= 1 returns 201 and the created book.
AC-2: POST /books with a missing title or an isbn that is not 13 digits returns 422.
AC-3: POST /books with an isbn that already exists returns 409.
AC-4: POST /members with a valid name and email returns 201.
AC-5: POST /members with an invalid email format returns 422.
AC-6: POST /members with an email that already exists returns 409.
AC-7: POST /loans with a valid book_id and member_id returns 201, and due_date equals loan date + 14 days.
AC-8: POST /loans for a book with 0 available copies returns 409.
AC-9: POST /loans for a member who already has 3 active loans returns 409.
AC-10: POST /loans with a non-existent book_id or member_id returns 404.
AC-11: POST /loans/{id}/return on an active loan returns 200 and sets returned_at.
AC-12: POST /loans/{id}/return on an already-returned loan returns 409.
AC-13: GET /books/{id} returns the book with its current available_copies; an unknown id returns 404.
AC-14: GET /loans/overdue returns only active loans whose due_date is before today.

Non-functional requirements:
- All errors return JSON with a "detail" field.
- No secrets in source code; configuration comes from environment variables.

