l format, unique case-insensitively | Required |\n+\n+## Loan\n+\n+Represents one borrowing event.\n+\n+| Field | Type/constraint | Notes |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| `id` | Unique identifier | Generated by the service |\n+| `book_id` | Existing Book reference | Required |\n+| `member_id` | Existing Member reference | Required |\n+| `loaned_at` | UTC timestamp | Set on successful creation |\n+| `due_date` | UTC calendar date | `loaned_at` date plus 14 days |\n+| `returned_at` | Nullable UTC timestamp | Unset while active |\n+\n+## Relationships and invariants\n+\n+- One Book has many Loans.\n+- One Member has many Loans.\n+- A Loan references exactly one Book and one Member.\n+- A loan is active when `returned_at` is unset.\n+- Active loans for a Book MUST NOT exceed `total_copies`.\n+- Active loans for a Member MUST NOT exceed 3.\n+- Returning a loan sets `returned_at` once; a second return is rejected.\n+- Books, Members, and Loans persist in the runtime SQLite database.\n*** Add File: specs/001-book-loan-service/contracts/openapi.yaml\n+openapi: 3.0.3\n+info:\n+  title: Library Book-Loan Service\n+  version: 1.0.0\n+  description: JSON HTTP API for catalog, membership, loans, returns, and overdue lookup.\n+paths:\n+  /books:\n+    post:\n+      operationId: createBook\n+      requestBody:\n+        required: true\n+        content:\n+          application/json:\n+            schema:\n+              $ref: '#/components/schemas/BookCreate'\n+      responses:\n+        '201':\n+          description: Created book\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Book'\n+        '409':\n+          description: ISBN already exists\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+        '422':\n+          description: Invalid book data\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+  /books/{id}:\n+    get:\n+      operationId: getBook\n+      parameters:\n+        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Id'\n+      responses:\n+        '200':\n+          description: Book with current availability\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Book'\n+        '404':\n+          description: Book not found\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+  /members:\n+    post:\n+      operationId: createMember\n+      requestBody:\n+        required: true\n+        content:\n+          application/json:\n+            schema:\n+              $ref: '#/components/schemas/MemberCreate'\n+      responses:\n+        '201':\n+          description: Created member\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Member'\n+        '409':\n+          description: Email already exists\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+        '422':\n+          description: Invalid member data\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+  /loans:\n+    post:\n+      operationId: createLoan\n+      requestBody:\n+        required: true\n+        content:\n+          application/json:\n+            schema:\n+              $ref: '#/components/schemas/LoanCreate'\n+      responses:\n+        '201':\n+          description: Created loan\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Loan'\n+        '404':\n+          description: Book or member not found\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+        '409':\n+          description: Book unavailable or member has three active loans\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+  /loans/{id}/return:\n+    post:\n+      operationId: returnLoan\n+      parameters:\n+        - $ref: '#/components/parameters/Id'\n+      responses:\n+        '200':\n+          description: Returned loan\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Loan'\n+        '404':\n+          description: Loan not found\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+        '409':\n+          description: Loan already returned\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                $ref: '#/components/schemas/Error'\n+  /loans/overdue:\n+    get:\n+      operationId: listOverdueLoans\n+      responses:\n+        '200':\n+          description: Active loans due before today\n+          content:\n+            application/json:\n+              schema:\n+                type: array\n+                items:\n+                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/Loan'\n+components:\n+  parameters:\n+    Id:\n+      name: id\n+      in: path\n+      required: true\n+      schema:\n+        type: integer\n+  schemas:\n+    BookCreate:\n+      type: object\n+      required: [title, author, isbn, total_copies]\n+      properties:\n+        title: {type: string}\n+        author: {type: string}\n+        isbn: {type: string, pattern: '^[0-9]{13}$'}\n+        total_copies: {type: integer, minimum: 1}\n+    Book:\n+      allOf:\n+        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/BookCreate'\n+        - type: object\n+          required: [id, available_copies]\n+          properties:\n+            id: {type: integer}\n+            available_copies: {type: integer, minimum: 0}\n+    MemberCreate:\n+      type: object\n+      required: [name, email]\n+      properties:\n+        name: {type: string}\n+        email: {type: string, format: email}\n+    Member:\n+      allOf:\n+        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/MemberCreate'\n+        - type: object\n+          required: [id]\n+          properties:\n+            id: {type: integer}\n+    LoanCreate:\n+      type: object\n+      required: [book_id, member_id]\n+      properties:\n+        book_id: {type: integer}\n+        member_id: {type: integer}\n+    Loan:\n+      type: object\n+      required: [id, book_id, member_id, loaned_at, due_date, returned_at]\n+      properties:\n+        id: {type: integer}\n+        book_id: {type: integer}\n+        member_id: {type: integer}\n+        loaned_at: {type: string, format: date-time}\n+        due_date: {type: string, format: date}\n+        returned_at: {type: string, format: date-time, nullable: true}\n+    Error:\n+      type: object\n+      required: [detail]\n+      properties:\n+        detail: {type: string}\n*** Add File: specs/001-book-loan-service/quickstart.md\n+# Quickstart Validation: Library Book-Loan Service\n+\n+## Prerequisites\n+\n+- Python 3.12\n+- Project dependencies installed from the project dependency manifest\n+- A writable runtime database path supplied through the configured environment\n+  variable\n+\n+## Run the service\n+\n+Set the runtime database configuration through the environment, then start the\n+FastAPI application using the project’s documented application entry point.\n+The service must use a file-backed SQLite database for runtime data.\n+\n+## Run acceptance tests\n+\n+Run pytest against `tests/`. The suite must contain exactly one primary test for\n+each acceptance criterion, with names containing `AC-1` through `AC-14`.\n+\n+Expected result: all mandatory tests pass and measured coverage is at least 80%.\n+\n+## Run quality gates\n+\n+Run the harness:\n+\n+```text\n+python .harness/run_harness.py\n+```\n+\n+The harness runs Ruff, Bandit, and pytest in that order. It writes each gate's\n+stdout, stderr, and exit code to a new `evidence/harness-results/run-N/`\n+directory and prints a final PASS/FAIL summary. Existing evidence directories\n+and recorded harness results must not be edited.\n+\n+## Manual contract checks\n+\n+The endpoint shapes, statuses, schemas, and error requirements are defined in\n+[contracts/openapi.yaml](contracts/openapi.yaml). Entity constraints and\n+state invariants are defined in [data-model.md](data-model.md).\n+\n+At minimum, verify:\n+\n+1. Create a valid book and member.\n+2. Create loans until inventory or the three-active-loan member limit is reached.\n+3. Return a loan and verify availability is restored.\n+4. Query overdue loans using records before, on, and after today's UTC date.\n+5. Restart the service and verify records remain available.\n*** Delete File: specs/001-book-loan-service/plan.md\n*** Add File: specs/001-book-loan-service/plan.md\n+# Implementation Plan: Library Book-Loan Service\n+\n+**Branch**: `001-book-loan-service` | **Date**: 2026-11-23 | **Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)\n+\n+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-book-loan-service/spec.md`\n+\n+## Summary\n+\n+Build a JSON HTTP library lending service using Python 3.12, FastAPI, and\n+SQLAlchemy. Runtime records use file-backed SQLite for restart persistence;\n+tests use isolated in-memory SQLite. The API implements catalog and member\n+creation, loan and return lifecycle rules, availability, overdue lookup, JSON\n+errors, and transactional limits. Ruff, Bandit, and pytest run through the\n+ordered `.harness/run_harness.py` evidence runner.\n+\n+## Technical Context\n+\n+**Language/Version**: Python 3.12\n+\n+**Primary Dependencies**: FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, pytest, httpx `TestClient`, Ruff,\n+Bandit\n+\n+**Storage**: SQLite file for runtime; SQLite in-memory database for tests\n+\n+**Testing**: pytest with httpx `TestClient`; one primary test per AC-1 through\n+AC-14, each test name containing its AC identifier\n+\n+**Target Platform**: Python service process on a supported server environment\n+\n+**Project Type**: Web service\n+\n+**Performance Goals**: Meet the supplied acceptance scenarios with ordinary\n+single-service SQLite workloads; no higher throughput target is specified.\n+\n+**Constraints**: All mandatory tests pass, coverage is at least 80%, Ruff has\n+zero errors, Bandit has zero medium/high findings, no hardcoded secrets, and\n+configuration is environment-driven. Existing harness evidence is immutable.\n+\n+**Scale/Scope**: Initial single-service library catalog and lending workflow;\n+no reservations, renewals, fines, notifications, deletion, or authentication.\n+\n+## Constitution Check\n+\n+*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*\n+\n+- **Small, purposeful changes**: PASS — implementation is limited to the\n+  requested API, tests, harness, and directly related SDD artifacts.\n+- **Preserve intended behavior**: PASS — contracts map directly to AC-1 through\n+  AC-14 and clarified rules.\n+- **Verify requirements with tests**: PASS — the plan requires one-to-one\n+  acceptance tests, mandatory test success, and at least 80% coverage.\n+- **Make failures explicit**: PASS — all API errors use JSON `detail`; runtime\n+  configuration is environment-driven and secrets are excluded.\n+- **Keep work reviewable**: PASS — source is under `src/`, tests under `tests/`,\n+  and harness evidence is append-only.\n+- **Ruff/Bandit gates**: PASS — the harness runs both without disabling rules.\n+- **SDD governance**: PASS — specification changes remain in the feature\n+  artifacts and are documented.\n+\n+## Phase 0: Research\n+\n+Research decisions are recorded in [research.md](research.md). They resolve the\n+requested framework, persistence, transaction, configuration, acceptance-test\n+mapping, and harness requirements.\n+\n+## Phase 1: Design\n+\n+Design artifacts:\n+\n+- [data-model.md](data-model.md) defines Book, Member, Loan, relationships, and\n+  invariants.\n+- [contracts/openapi.yaml](contracts/openapi.yaml) defines all public routes,\n+  request/response shapes, statuses, and JSON errors.\n+- [quickstart.md](quickstart.md) defines end-to-end validation and harness\n+  evidence expectations.\n+\n+## Project Structure\n+\n+### Documentation\n+\n+```text\n+specs/001-book-loan-service/\n+├── plan.md\n+├── research.md\n+├── data-model.md\n+├── contracts/\n+│   └── openapi.yaml\n+├── quickstart.md\n+└── tasks.md\n+```\n+\n+### Source Code\n+\n+```text\n+src/\n+├── library_service/\n+│   ├── __init__.py\n+│   ├── config.py\n+│   ├── database.py\n+│   ├── models.py\n+│   ├── schemas.py\n+│   ├── services.py\n+│   ├── api.py\n+│   └── main.py\n+\n+tests/\n+├── conftest.py\n+└── test_book_loan_api.py\n+\n+.harness/\n+└── run_harness.py\n+\n+evidence/\n+└── harness-results/\n+    └── run-N/\n+```\n+\n+**Structure Decision**: Use one Python web-service package under `src/` with\n+separate configuration, database, persistence models, API schemas, business\n+services, and application assembly. Keep acceptance tests in one focused module\n+with shared fixtures. Keep the harness separate from application code and write\n+new evidence runs without altering prior results.\n+\n+## Implementation Notes\n+\n+- Configure the runtime SQLite URL through an environment variable and expose\n+  dependency overrides for the in-memory test database.\n+- Use database uniqueness constraints for ISBN and case-insensitive member\n+  email, translating conflicts to 409 responses.\n+- Use explicit transaction boundaries around loan eligibility checks and loan\n+  insertion; ensure concurrent requests cannot oversubscribe inventory or the\n+  member limit.\n+- Centralize JSON error handling so validation, not-found, conflict, and\n+  unexpected service errors follow the `detail` contract.\n+- Keep date calculations in UTC: `due_date